<title>POLAND: Polish macroeconomic forecast for Feb-April 1997.</title>
<headline>Polish macroeconomic forecast for Feb-April 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a macreconomic forecast for the first quarter of 1997, submitted February 20, prepared for Reuters by Tadeusz Chroscicki, chief analyst at the Government's Centre for Strategic Studies (CSS):</p>
<p>MAIN ECONOMIC INDICATOR FORECAST</p>
<p>				JANUARY    FEBRUARY    MARCH	APRIL</p>
<p>CPI (pct change)</p>
<p>  month/month		2.9(R)   2.0 (1.8)    1.4	    1.0</p>
<p>  year/year		 18.1(R)  18.7(18.1)   18.6(18.0)   17.2</p>
<p>  Previous Dec = 100   102.9(R) 104.6(105.0) 106.4(106.1) 107.5</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT</p>
<p>  month/month	     -3.4(R)   -3.0	  10.0	    0.0</p>
<p>  year/year		  8.6(R)    8.8(9.0)    9.0(11.0)    8.5</p>
<p> UNEMPLOYMENT RATE(pct)13.5-13.6  13.6(13.8)  13.6(13.9)   13.5</p>
<p>Following figures in billion USD</p>
<p> OFFICIAL RESERVES     18.2(18.0)  18.0(17.9)  17.9(17.6)  17.8</p>
<p> NET RESERVES	    21.5(21.8)  21.6(21.7)  21.5	  21.4</p>
<p> C/A TRADE BALANCE*     -1.0	  -1.5	 -3.0	  -3.5</p>
<p>  Exports*		   1.9	   4.0	  6.0	   8.2</p>
<p>  Imports*		   2.9	   5.5	  9.0	  11.7</p>
<p>		    *********************************</p>
<p>NOTES: Revised figures in brackets. Official forex reserves are hard currencies held by the central bank while net reserves are the total amount of foreign exchange in the banking system. Indicators marked (R) are results, rest are forecasts.</p>
<p>* Counted from start of year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700, fax +48 22 653 9780</p>
